  steps:
  - label: Font Face
    targets:
    - Fonts
    - Size
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 53
      y: 105
      width: 169
      height: 38
    message: Font Picker lets you change your text design. Use Serif fonts like Times
      New Roman for print and Sans-serif fonts like Arial for digital.
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Font Size
    targets:
    - SpaceBefore
    - SpaceAfter
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 221
      y: 105
      width: 60
      height: 38
    message: 'Font Size establishes a clear visual hierarchy using points (pt). It
      controls how large or small your text appears. '
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Text Emphasis
    targets:
    - SpaceBefore
    - SpaceAfter
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 282
      y: 105
      width: 73
      height: 38
    message: "Text Emphasis highlights important words and guides the reader\u2019s
      attention. Use it sparingly to keep text clear."
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Bold
    targets:
    - Bold
    - Italic
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 282
      y: 105
      width: 36
      height: 38
    message: Bold makes text thicker and darker. It is used to emphasize important
      words, key concepts, and headings.
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Italic
    targets:
    - SpaceBefore
    - SpaceAfter
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 318
      y: 105
      width: 36
      height: 38
    message: Italic text slants to the right and is used for titles of major works,
      foreign terms, or subtle emphasis on specific words.
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Alignment
    targets:
    - SpaceBefore
    - SpaceAfter
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 364
      y: 105
      width: 108
      height: 38
    message: 'Text alignment determines how your paragraphs line up against the margins
      of your document. '
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Left Alignment
    targets:
    - Left
    - Center
    - Right
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 364
      y: 105
      width: 36
      height: 38
    message: Left-aligned text has a straight left edge and a ragged right edge.
      It is standard for academic writing.
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Center Alignment
    targets:
    - SpaceBefore
    - SpaceAfter
    useExplicitArea: 1
    area:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 400
      y: 105
      width: 36
      height: 38
    message: Center-aligned text places words in the middle of the page. It is mainly
      used for titles, cover pages, and section headers.
    overridePadding: 1
    padding: 2
    placement: 0
    pennyOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
    holeIsClickThrough: 1
  - label: Right Alignment
